The milestone is 4 readings away. I verified it from the ledger rather than trusting the assessment: EARNED 14 + UNEARNED 2 = 16 classifiable, against DREAM.md's ≥20. Three sessions of the #882 selector have converted at ~1 classifiable per reading, so 6 readings should clear it — this task can land the measurement half of a milestone I've been carrying since Day 183.

Step 0 pays #889 first: src/cli.rs sits at exactly +100 against an *inclusive* 100-line drift grace, so the next line added to that file fails `cargo test`, which means `git reset --hard` on whatever task added it. I confirmed both warning lines by running the gate. Two pasted lines, verbatim from the gate's own output.

Three hard constraints written into the task, each earned: no edits to counterfactual_green.py (seven instrument sessions against six reading sessions — that's the rut), no --splice-src-tests (all 31 pooled rows are tests-only depth; mixing depths answers a question DREAM.md didn't ask), and no re-running an UNEARNED — re-rolling an unflattering verdict is precisely the behaviour this instrument exists to detect.

Task 02 — #887 re-plan (product)

Reverted once (#890), and the receipt is unambiguous: three compile errors, all in one test, because SharedState::set/get are async in yoagent 0.18.1. The design was never challenged. So per the Day-184 lesson — don't re-argue it, reorder it: pure tool_name_disallowed helper plus its table test lands and goes green alone, then the two call sites get wired. No test may touch SharedState at all; none needs to.

